{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2141-01-29 23:55:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hello, I'm Dr. Lee. I'll be taking care of you tonight. Can you tell me what brought you to the hospital?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2141-01-29 23:56:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Hi, Doctor. I’ve been feeling a bit off. My blood sugar was really high yesterday—over 400. I called my PCP and he said to come in."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2141-01-29 23:57:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I see. You have type 1 diabetes, correct? And you're on insulin?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2141-01-29 23:58:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, I take glargine and humalog. I gave myself 8 units of humalog at home, but it didn’t bring it down much."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2141-01-29 23:59:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Okay. Any symptoms like nausea, vomiting, or trouble breathing?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2141-01-30 00:00:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "No, nothing like that. Just a little tired and not as hungry as usual."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2141-01-30 00:01:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Got it. We also noticed your white blood cell count is low. It’s 1.7, which is below normal. That’s called neutropenia. Have you felt feverish or had any signs of infection?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2141-01-30 00:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "No fever. I feel okay now. Could that be from my meds?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2141-01-30 00:03:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s possible. You’re on valganciclovir and ertapenem—both can lower white counts. We’re going to stop those for now since we don’t see signs of active infection."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2141-01-30 00:04:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Oh, okay. I was worried it might be something serious."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2141-01-30 00:05:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re checking everything. We did a chest X-ray, and it shows stable heart size—no pneumonia or fluid. That’s good."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2141-01-30 00:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve had heart issues before. EF is 40%, and I have a pacemaker."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2141-01-30 00:07:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, I see that. Your heart is stable now. We’ll keep monitoring. We also ordered blood cultures and a CMV test to make sure there’s no virus or bacteria."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2141-01-30 00:08:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I remember last time I was in for infection after transplant. I don’t want that again."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2141-01-30 00:09:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I understand. But right now, you’re not showing signs of sepsis. No fever, lungs are clear, and you feel well. We’re being cautious."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2141-01-30 06:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. Your vitals are stable. Temperature is normal, and you’re breathing well."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2141-01-30 06:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Morning, Doctor. How are my labs?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2141-01-30 06:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your blood sugar this morning is 270—still high, but better. We’ll keep your insulin going as scheduled."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2141-01-30 06:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I did drink some peach nectar yesterday. Maybe that’s why it spiked."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2141-01-30 06:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That could definitely contribute. We’ll talk about adjusting your insulin later, but for now, we’re keeping your usual doses."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2141-01-30 06:05:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your tacrolimus level came back at 11.3—perfect range. So your transplant is well-covered."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2141-01-30 06:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Good. I take that twice a day with my cellcept."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2141-01-30 06:07:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, and we’re continuing both. We stopped valganciclovir yesterday to help your white count recover."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2141-01-30 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We got your urine culture back—no growth. That’s reassuring."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2141-01-30 10:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So no infection in the urine?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2141-01-30 10:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "No. And your blood cultures are negative so far. CMV test came back with no virus detected."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2141-01-30 10:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s a relief. What about the low white count?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2141-01-30 10:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It’s improving—now up to 2.0. ANC is 1300. We think it was due to the meds, not an active infection."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2141-01-30 10:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So I can stop worrying about that?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2141-01-30 10:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "For now, yes. We’ll keep watching, but it’s moving in the right direction."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2141-01-30 15:55:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We did an ultrasound of your liver today. You have cirrhosis, which we knew about, but no new issues—no fluid or blockages."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2141-01-30 15:56:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "From past drinking, yeah. But I’ve been sober for years."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2141-01-30 15:57:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good to hear. The scan shows no signs of decompensation, so we’ll keep you on a low-sodium diet as before."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2141-01-30 15:58:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my kidney? The transplant is okay?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2141-01-30 15:59:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, no hydronephrosis. Your creatinine is 1.1—back to your baseline. Graft is functioning well."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2141-01-31 07:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good news—we’re planning to discharge you today. Your labs are stable, and you feel well."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2141-01-31 07:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s great. What about my meds?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2141-01-31 07:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ll continue tacrolimus, cellcept, dapsone, and your insulin. We stopped valganciclovir and ertapenem permanently."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2141-01-31 07:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And the micafungin? I’m still on IV antifungal."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2141-01-31 07:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, continue micafungin at home for the full course. Home health will help with that."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2141-01-31 07:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my blood sugar? Should I adjust insulin?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2141-01-31 07:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Keep your current dose for now. Follow up with your endocrinologist—they may adjust it based on home readings."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2141-01-31 07:07:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Weigh yourself daily. Call if you gain more than 3 pounds—could be fluid from heart or kidney issues."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2141-01-31 07:08:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ll do that. Any other signs to watch for?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2141-01-31 07:09:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Fever, shortness of breath, or swelling. But you’re in good shape. Just keep up with your transplant and ID follow-ups."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2141-01-31 07:10:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you, Doctor. I feel much better knowing it wasn’t another infection."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2141-01-31 07:11:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. We’ll get your discharge papers ready. You should be home within a few hours."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2141-01-31 07:12:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Appreciate all the care."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2141-01-31 07:13:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Take care. And keep up the good work with your health."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2141-01-31 07:14:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will do."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2141-01-29 23:54:00",
